  "rationale": "Blakey's first Riverside album, with the peak 1961-1964 Jazz Messengers lineup: Hubbard, Shorter, Fuller, Walton, Workman. BBC calls it 'hard bop at its finest'; AllMusic Guide says it's Blakey's best work. The title track (Juan Tizol standard) and Shorter's 'This Is for Albert' are essential. Consensus across Penguin Guide (3\u2605), AllMusic (4.5\u2605), DownBeat (4\u2605), Rolling Stone Jazz Guide (4\u2605). Fills a key gap \u2014 Blakey's Riverside period is underrepresented in the canon.",
